title: Founder approved live Claude-in-sandbox test on subscription; next steps owed to the founder listed
summary: |-
  The founder approved running the Claude-compat check on their subscription (two short turns). Method:
  - The same `claude -p` turn runs unsandboxed as a control and under the hardened macOS session profile (§15.5 plus the sysmond mach-lookup deny and the tmux unix-socket deny).
  - The model only runs check.sh; ground truth is the script's own out.txt.
  - Criteria: Claude authenticates and answers; Bash can write in the workdir, spawn/kill a child, and run node. Under the sandbox, the stand-in endpoint port is unreachable, pgrep sees nothing, and the denied dir is unwritable.

  Probe: packages/gnomon/probes/p10m-claude-compat.

  Still owed by the founder:
  - relay host (OPEN 16);
  - whether the LaunchServices `open` escape is accepted as a residual covered by presence;
  - the Developer ID provisioning profile for gnomon.helper;
  - the App Store Connect API key plus `notarytool store-credentials gnomon-notary`;
  - Windows PC setup (Hello, standard user, access).
